# 29. L2 Change Summary

## Change

Create a restricted sudoers configuration for:

```text
um501001
```

to manage:

```text
api-reporter.service
```

on the Production RCM servers.

## Reason

The requirement was identified during API Reporter deployment and validation in UAT/TE2.

The technical account requires elevated privileges for specific `systemctl` service-management operations but must not receive general root access.

Production must be aligned with the successfully validated UAT/TE2 configuration.

## Scope

Production RCM servers hosting the API Reporter.

## Security

The change follows the principle of least privilege.

Only explicitly approved `systemctl` commands for `api-reporter` are permitted.

No unrestricted sudo/root access is granted.

## Pre-Deployment Validation

```bash
sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/api-reporter
sudo -l -U um501001
```

## Post-Deployment Validation

```bash
sudo systemctl status api-reporter
systemctl is-enabled api-reporter
ps -ef | grep '[a]pi-reporter'
ss -lntp | grep 8000
```

## Rollback

```bash
sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/api-reporter
sudo visudo -c
```

---

# 30. Important Recommendation

Before implementing the Production configuration, compare it with the existing configuration already validated in UAT/TE2:

```bash
sudo grep -Rni "um501001\|api-reporter" /etc/sudoers.d/
```

Then display the relevant UAT/TE2 file:

```bash
sudo cat /etc/sudoers.d/<existing-api-reporter-sudoers-file>
```

The Production configuration should replicate the validated UAT/TE2 configuration wherever possible.
